  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling up health emergency response interventions to flooding and cholera in 8 most affected counties in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to scale up health emergency response interventions to flooding and cholera in the eight most affected counties in Kenya. WHO focuses on preventing and managing vector and water-borne diseases such as Malaria, Rift Valley fever, Dengue fever, Cholera, and vaccine-preventable diseases like Measles in these flood-affected counties. WHO strengthens early warning and disease surveillance through rapid response teams and community health promoters to conduct outbreak investigations and initiate response interventions. The response supports national and county coordination for a multisectoral approach, including the distribution of WHO emergency health kits and essential medical supplies. WHO targets 58,237 people, including 11,647 women, 5,832 men, and 40,767 children.</narrative>
  </description>
